{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793040742,"nonce":"nN++aNtqMieJWo4lr9gq6DqauHk=","title":"Restore unsaved CRDT buffers without replacing saved workspace files","message":"The current doc.restore writes checkpoint text to disk and normal background/release/shutdown flushes also write shared text. Add an explicit control-plane buffered restore mode with an expected saved-file SHA-256. Keep the existing replace mode compatible. Persist a versioned, checksummed private record containing the graph and disk baseline so reopen/restart retains unsaved text without interpreting the saved file as a newer edit. Background flush, last-subscriber release and shutdown must persist this graph without saving it to the project file.\n\nExplicit Save verifies the disk baseline first. A write-ahead state record must distinguish a save interrupted before and after the disk write, without losing either version or treating an unrelated outside write as a successful save. Recovered buffers continue requiring explicit Save. Reject direct writes that would overwrite a dirty recovered buffer, including after its live view has been released. Preserve graph identity and reject corrupt/incomplete records, bad modes/digests, changed/missing/non-text baselines, unauthorized restore and active aliases.\n\nExpose buffered/dirty metadata on document open and a bufferedRestore capability; browser-forwarded restore remains denied. Validate native fault boundaries, restart, outside edits, explicit saves, legacy compatibility and local hosted journal recovery. Rebuild WASM and native session and refresh the existing local services after the milestone.\n\nThis is saved-file/buffer separation for the restoration seam, not complete filesystem reconstruction or automatic VM recovery. Path movement/stable identities, initial filesystem and Git manifests, external-write reconciliation, compute leases/fencing and MSB provisioning remain under 52138fcda83502ec87679713955f7cf7c7f7e8654a0ef55ba60357bd0f22a904 and 670bd15d5f2a4c8fdd82da62e9b72599f9a689affc5682a7b621f81fd72156c0. Real Cloudflare deployment is not needed for local validation; notify the user when account resources are required.","files":null}]}